{% comment %}
  Cover for the TBI series: a brain drawn as a network. Points are a farthest-point sample of the fsaverage5 left pial
  surface (lateral view, via nilearn), each joined to its three nearest neighbours; the warm patches mark where a
  frontal blow bruises the brain (coup) and where it rebounds (contrecoup).
{% endcomment %}
<style>
  .tbi-cover { position: absolute; inset: 1.5rem 1.5rem 3.4rem; color: var(--global-theme-color); --tbi-cover-hot: #d9483b; }
  html[data-theme="dark"] .tbi-cover { --tbi-cover-hot: #ff6b5c; }
  .tbi-cover-svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }
  .tbi-cover-edges line { stroke: currentColor; stroke-opacity: 0.26; stroke-width: 1; }
  .tbi-cover-edges line.is-warm { stroke: var(--tbi-cover-hot); stroke-opacity: 0.3; }
  .tbi-cover-edges line.is-hot { stroke: var(--tbi-cover-hot); stroke-opacity: 0.6; }
  .tbi-cover-nodes circle { fill: currentColor; fill-opacity: 0.72; }
  .tbi-cover-nodes circle.is-warm { fill: var(--tbi-cover-hot); fill-opacity: 0.6; }
  .tbi-cover-nodes circle.is-hot { fill: var(--tbi-cover-hot); fill-opacity: 0.95; }
  .tbi-cover-halo { animation: tbi-cover-pulse 4.5s ease-in-out infinite; transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center; }
  .tbi-cover-halo.is-late { animation-delay: 0.6s; }
  @keyframes tbi-cover-pulse { 0%, 100% { opacity: 0.55; transform: scale(0.92); } 50% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1.05); } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .tbi-cover-halo { animation: none; } }
</style>
